## Post-Write Self-Check Checklist

After writing code, verify every item:
- [ ] **No `any` or loose `unknown` casts** — 100% strict TypeScript.
- [ ] **No hardcoded palette colors** — all colors use semantic tokens (`bg-primary`, `text-foreground`, `border-border`, etc.).
- [ ] **No hardcoded user-facing strings or aria-labels** — all copy uses `t(...)` with parity in `messages/en.json` and `messages/ar.json`.
- [ ] **No physical left/right CSS** — all spacing/positioning uses Tailwind logical properties (`ps-`, `pe-`, `ms-`, `me-`, `start-`, `end-`, `text-start`, `text-end`).
- [ ] **Directional icons flip in RTL** — chevrons/arrows include `rtl:rotate-180`.
- [ ] **Store context attached** — all API calls ensure `setApiStoreId` / `resolveRequestStore` is invoked for `X-Store-Id`.
- [ ] **Independent server fetches parallelized** — using `Promise.all` or `Promise.allSettled`.
- [ ] **XSS protected** — all HTML rendering uses `SafeHtmlRenderer` (DOMPurify) and JSON-LD uses `serializeJsonLd()`.
- [ ] **Money formatted correctly** — using `formatCurrency(amount, currency, locale)`.
- [ ] **Package manager is Yarn** — never run `npm`.

If any violation exists, fix it immediately before presenting to the user.
